[I] A secure utmp/wtmp implementation

[T] utmps is a library by skarnet implementing the utmpx.h family of
[T] functions for C libraries that lack them, such as musl, or implement
[T] them insecurely. It does not rely on setuid or setgid programs; instead
[T] a daemon manages the utmp data and the utmpx primitives communicate with
[T] it.

[U] https://skarnet.org/software/utmps/

[A] Utmps Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/base
[F] CROSS

[V] 0.1.3.4
[L] ISC

[D] b0e4ba30c8edd6393372a41dfd61076ccc76eacd7b05d8ac86196f83 utmps-0.1.3.4.tar.gz https://skarnet.org/software/utmps/

atstage cross && var_append confopt ' ' "--with-sysdeps=$root$libdir/skalibs/sysdeps --with-lib=$root$libdir --with-dynlib=$root$libdir"
